@@ -314,6 +314,19 @@ includes compact `Claim:` and `Evidence:` lines when available.
 or cancellation returns a tool error rather than an empty result, and stops
 the ongoing page scan. For a known page, use `wiki_get` with its id or path.
 
+Before changing a synthesis, call `wiki_get` with `includeMetadata: true`.
+Its text result is JSON containing the page body, pagination, and complete
+mutation metadata: `sourceIds`, `claims` with evidence, `contradictions`,
+`questions`, and optional `confidence` and `status`. Metadata is not paginated;
+`fromLine` and `lineCount` still apply to the body. Read remaining body pages
+when `truncated` is true. Ordinary calls keep their body-only text output.
+Memory-corpus fallback has no wiki mutation metadata. This option does not
+change page visibility or allow filesystem access.
+
+A synthesis update replaces `sourceIds` and any supplied `claims` array. Retain
+unrelated citations and claim evidence, omit unchanged optional arrays, and
+preserve the page status. Do not infer complete metadata from search snippets.
+
 The plugin also registers a non-exclusive memory corpus supplement, so shared
 `memory_search` and `memory_get` can reach the wiki when the active memory
 plugin supports corpus selection.
